Subject Areas Education Nursing Social Sciences Natural Sciences & Mathematics Humanities Health Care Fine & Performing Arts Communications Computer Science & Technology Business & Leadership Admissions Admissions Campus Admissions Online Admissions Nursing Admissions Transfer to Baker Adult Learners Admitted Students Tuition & Aid Tuition & Aid Campus Tuition & Aid Online Tuition & Aid Nursing Tuition & Aid Scholarships Military & Veteran Benefits Apply for Financial Aid (FAFSA) Paying for College Work Study Student Experience Student Experience Campus & Residential Life Fraternity & Sorority Life Online Learning Experience Academic and Career Success Diversity & Inclusion About Baker About Baker Leadership History & Traditions Accreditations & Standards Professional Licensure Information Careers at Baker Contact Us News For You Info for: Current Students Faculty & Staff Parents & Families Alumni Quick Links News Events Moodle MyBaker Portal Help Desk Request Transcript Fac & Staff Intranet Registrar Course Catalogs Academic Calendar Library Baker Email Home Student Experience Academic and Career Success Academic and Career Success At Baker, we don’t just help students earn As. We’re with you every step of the way to make sure everything you do leads to real-world success. Visit Baker Connect with an admissions counselor Main navigation Menu: Home Home Academic and Career Success Campus & Residential Life Fraternity & Sorority Life Online Learning Experience Diversity & Inclusion Home Academic and Career Success Campus & Residential Life Fraternity & Sorority Life Online Learning Experience Diversity & Inclusion Table of Contents Your Success Here Becomes Your Success Anywhere The Success of Our Students Speaks for Itself Already Imagining Yourself at Baker? Your Success Here Becomes Your Success Anywhere Here, your college experience and career journey start on the same day. From choosing your major to finding an internship, we collaborate with you to create the life you imagine after graduation. Here’s how we help give your academic life real-world meaning. A Guided Journey From Resume-Building to Internships and Beyond Landing a dream job is about more than job-ready knowledge. It’s about discovering your talents and where you can make an impact. It’s about the way you represent yourself. It can be scary. It can seem complicated. Our supportive career services team helps shape your plan, develop your resume, and find hands-on experience. Career Services Academic Advising That Helps You Truly Understand Coursework Let’s co-create an academic journey that challenges you and supports your dreams. Peer tutoring. Academic coaching. Accessibility and accommodations. We’ll partner with you to make sense of the material so you not only pass, but truly understand . Academic Support and Advising The Success of Our Students Speaks for Itself Your hard work and talent got you here. Add our passion for personalized student support, and you’ll go far. Here’s what you can expect from your Baker education. Highest Average Income Our graduates earn more on average than graduates from any other Kansas university. 99% Placement Rate Nearly 99% of our graduates land a job or get accepted into  graduate school. Highest ROI in Kansas More than any other private university in the state. Our graduates translate their education into value. Already Imagining Yourself at Baker? We can’t wait to meet you and show you around! Schedule a visit and meet your Wildcat success team—professors, advisors, and future classmates. You’ll experience first-hand why our campuses feel like home. And students who make an in-person visit to our Baldwin City campus are eligible for a $1,000 Visit Grant when they enroll. Can be combined with Academic Merit Scholarships, not Athletic. Schedule your visit today Scholars Symposium: How Your Academic Success Pays Off Every April, Baker faculty hand-picks students for $240,000+ in additional scholarships. No need to apply. Just do what you do best—excel. Add those scholarships to the $31,000 average aid package for Baker undergraduates. It’s all part of how we make your education affordable. Scholarships Image Get Advice From Experienced Professionals in Your Field Our award-winning faculty already bring real-world experience to the classroom. Every year, we also have opportunities for students to hear directly from alumni and field experts. Searls Speaker Series Each semester, 5-7 Baker alumni share their paths to business success. They’ll discuss first-hand experiences and offer advice. Psychology Alumni Panel Held at least once a year, these seminars focus on the work experience of Baker graduates. Students will learn how to make an impact with a psychology degree. Pre-Health Panel Every November, a panel of Baker health care alumni talk about their journeys. They’ll share everything they wish they knew as students. And they’ll share how they navigate their careers today. Subscribe to our LinkedIn Career Services Newsletter We’re always working hard to develop our students and help them launch careers. Our Baker U Career Services LINK newsletter shares upcoming seminars, career fairs, internship opportunities, and more. Career Services Newsletter Request Information Apply to Baker Plan Your Visit Degrees & Programs Connect with us: facebook instagram linkedin youtube tiktok Phone (785) 594-6451 Get Directions Campus Safety & Alerts Careers Wildcat Wearhouse Alumni Baker University prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, sex, religion, age, disability, marital status, veteran status, pregnancy status, sexual orientation, or other status protected by law in the university’s programs and activities. Retaliation is also prohibited by university policy. Title IX Privacy Policy Consumer Information Compliance Reporting Accreditation © Copyright 2026 Baker University Back to top"
